  pure Rust software floating-point arithmetic, including x87 extended precision.
  https://github.com/rust-lang/rustc_apfloat
- smallvec 1.16.2 (MIT OR Apache-2.0) — transitive dependency of rustc_apfloat.
  https://github.com/servo/rust-smallvec
- bitflags 2.13.2 (MIT OR Apache-2.0) — transitive dependency of rustc_apfloat.
  https://github.com/bitflags/bitflags
- iced-x86 1.21.0 (MIT) — installation-time x86 decoder, decoder/instr_info
  features only; no assembler or runtime machine-code generation.
  https://github.com/icedland/iced
  Source commit: c50f29b7bc305696895c075f3fc7719751426b12.
  Copyright (C) 2018-present iced project and contributors.
- lazy_static 1.5.1 (MIT OR Apache-2.0; MIT selected) — iced-x86 dependency.
  https://github.com/rust-lang-nursery/lazy-static.rs
- sha2 0.10.9 (MIT OR Apache-2.0; MIT selected) — source EXE SHA-256 binding.
  https://github.com/RustCrypto/hashes
- digest 0.10.7 and crypto-common 0.1.7 (MIT OR Apache-2.0; MIT selected) —
  sha2 traits and common types. https://github.com/RustCrypto/traits
- block-buffer 0.10.4 and cpufeatures 0.2.17 (MIT OR Apache-2.0; MIT selected) —
  sha2 buffering and host feature detection. https://github.com/RustCrypto/utils
- generic-array 0.14.7 (MIT) — sha2 transitive dependency.
  https://github.com/fizyk20/generic-array
- typenum 1.20.1 (MIT OR Apache-2.0; MIT selected) — sha2 transitive dependency.
  https://github.com/paholg/typenum
- cfg-if 1.0.5 (MIT OR Apache-2.0; MIT selected) — host feature selection.
  https://github.com/rust-lang/cfg-if
- version_check 0.9.5 (MIT/Apache-2.0; MIT selected) — build dependency of
  generic-array, not a guest runtime compiler. https://github.com/SergioBenitez/version_check
- System libiconv (platform-provided) — CP932/UTF-8/Windows-1252 conversion,
  linked from the host OS rather than vendored. The exact implementation and
  version follow the platform. https://www.gnu.org/software/libiconv/

- System AppKit.framework and CoreGraphics.framework (platform-provided) —
  public macOS window/event and CPU image presentation APIs. No Apple source
  is copied. The optional visible backend is linked on macOS only.

## Test dependencies (not linked into wire)

- System JavaScriptCore.framework (platform-provided) — public C API used by
  the experimental macOS Wasm probe/runner only. No WebKit source is vendored
  or copied, and the framework is not currently linked into the wire binary.
  Framework version follows the OS. https://developer.apple.com/documentation/javascriptcore
- unicorn-engine / unicorn-engine-sys 2.1.5 (GPL-2.0) — differential-test
  reference emulator and lockstep debugging example only.
  https://github.com/unicorn-engine/unicorn

